From: Flowery development
Subject: [PATCH] UAC2: accept read-only Clock Source when GET_RANGE advertises the requested rate

Many class-compliant DACs expose a fixed or non-host-programmable Clock
Source and select sample rate via the AudioStreaming alternate setting.
Requiring GET_CUR to already match the track rate caused USB exclusive
playback to fail with "source frequency is read-only" for common 44.1/96 kHz
libraries.

GET_RANGE remains the capability gate. SET_CUR is issued only when the
source frequency control is host-programmable (bmControls frequency bits
0b10). Unit tests and the bit-perfect path audit document the policy.
---

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/waizusora/flowery/UsbLibusbSession.kt b/app/src/main/java/com/waizusora/flowery/UsbLibusbSession.kt
